                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "Appreciate the snippet. It \"sort of\" works, but not quite as expected. Consider the following:\r\n\r\n- 3 _buffers_ opened in 3 _tabs_. nVim is showing tab 3:\r\n  <img width=\"887\" height=\"70\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/881c7d8a-fcf9-405e-ab23-751917e5fecf\" />\r\n\r\n- I execute `my_wipeout()`. Expected result: 2 tabs left with `filetypes.lua` (2nd tab) being active. Actual result: \r\n  <img width=\"513\" height=\"68\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2c6c5f44-3a2e-400b-a867-de127ac48c80\" />\r\n\r\nHow come?.. Let's check the `:buffers`:\r\n```\r\n:buffers\r\n  1 %a   \"mini.lua\"                     line 8\r\n  3  h   \"diff.lua\"                     line 4\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo, instead of `diff.lua` which was loaded in tab 3, the `my_wipeout()` removed inactive buffer `filetypes.lua`! Quite a twist.",
